{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_quorum_restart_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"81237e6441414088bfb2079263cc63ec-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Adds a third phase for the failing mode: after the simultaneous flagged restart leaves all three voters with empty configurations and no leader, the same three nodes are stopped and restarted once more on the same durable stores with RestoreCommittedLogs disabled, and the probe records their configurations and whether a leader is elected. The earlier phases, observations and comparisons are unchanged; two comparisons are added for the operator restart.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"follower_abort\\\",\\\"heartbeat_timeout_election\\\",\\\"cfg_doc\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Three-voter in-process cluster at protocol version 3 with 50ms heartbeat/election timeouts: bootstrap on A, replication to B and C, ten commits, no snapshot, simultaneous graceful shutdown of all three, restart with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled (failing mode) or disabled (control). In the failing mode the probe then stops the three nodes again and restarts them with the flag disabled on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances and fresh transports, recording each node's configuration and whether a leader appears within eight seconds.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The second restart differs from the first only in the flag, so any change in the outcome is attributable to the restart path rather than to the stores, which are the same instances.\\\",\\\"The operator restart is the natural remediation an operator would attempt after noticing the empty configurations, and it does not require discarding the durable state.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No RecoverCluster in this harness: the operator paths on a stopped node are covered by the dedicated single-voter harness and its receipt.\\\",\\\"The control mode keeps its original two phases, so its earlier comparisons retain their meaning.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":3,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"recovery_opportunity_seconds\\\":8}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real replication, real commits, real graceful shutdowns and restarts on the same stores with fresh transports; the recovery phase uses the same stores and the same configuration with the flag disabled, and no other change.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_recovery\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_recovery_leader\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"nodes_with_full_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After a simultaneous restart with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, all three voters must still know the configuration whose entry is present in their own committed logs.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"nodes_with_full_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same simultaneous restart without the flag keeps all three voters configured.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"operator_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_recovery\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"nodes_with_full_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Restarting the same nodes with the flag disabled must restore the configuration on every voter, so the in-memory loss is reversible without discarding durable state.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"operator_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_recovery_leader\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"any_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After that operator restart the cluster must be able to elect a leader again.\\\"}\n ]\n}\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"The operator remediation for the cluster-wide case is being executed: a construction-time run of the extended simultaneous-restart harness reproduced the empty configurations and no leader, then stopped the same three nodes and restarted them on the same stores with the flag disabled, after which all three reported the configuration again and a leader was elected within eight seconds. Its retained receipt is requested in this update; if it holds, the headline progress loss is in-memory only and reversible by an ordinary restart, which bounds its impact.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
